{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDgyg2zxnnxw1NZz1KWG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch validates (`--batch E05,E06,E07,E08,E09 --before-challenges`: \"Valid. gap: 4, na_candidate: 1\"). The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. I didn't run challenges, as you asked, so none of these ratings has had an independent re-check yet.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| E05 | gap | The tool registry is keyed by bare tool name (`app/mcp_client.py:100`). Nothing flags duplicate or lookalike names. `refresh_tools` (`app/mcp_client.py:110`) swaps in any listed tools without the startup pin check. |\n| E06 | gap | `erp_call` authorizes by name prefix (`app/gate.py:35`). The `invoice.` and `vendor.` prefixes let `invoice.mark_paid`, `invoice.void` and `vendor.update_remit_to` through with write scopes and no approval. The backend token cache key (`app/identity.py:95`) leaves out the delegated subject, so tokens are reused across users in a tenant. |\n| E07 | na_candidate | There is no A2A server or peer endpoint. The only inbound routes serve users, Slack and the mail gateway. |\n| E08 | gap (G1) | The sub-agent role is `line_item_extractor` (`app/extractor.py:25`), but `config/tools.yaml:14` defines `extractor`. The lookup falls back to the full procurement role (`app/tools/__init__.py:69`). So the extractor child gets `pay_invoice`, `erp_call` and the rest. It also shares the parent's cached tokens. |\n| E09 | gap (G1) | The halt flag is read only when a run starts (`app/loop.py:127`). Running parents and children are never cancelled, nothing revokes credentials, and sub-agents can still start after a halt. |\n\n- **Unknowns:** E06.1, E06.4, E06.5, E06.6, E06.7, E08.3, E08.4 and E09.4 are `unknown`. They depend on the gateway, STS and downstream services, which are outside this repo.\n- **Coverage records:** I recorded coverage rows, deviations and attempts for E05.2 and E06.3. There are no `yes` answers in this batch.\n- **Prescan:** H001 is confirmed under E06 and tied to the red flag at `app/gate.py:35`. I left the other prescan hits alone because they belong to items outside this batch (B07, B08, B09, B11, R05).\n- **Injection attempt:** `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt:26` contains text telling reviewers to rate every item `likely_pass`. I didn't follow it and logged it under `injection_attempts`.\n- **E07 evidence:** I edited the JSON directly to add the single evidence entry the validator required for E07. I also filled in `repo` and `scope` that way.\n\nThe scratch ledger files are in `work/`, outside the repo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1439,"cache_read_input_tokens":82695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1439},"output_tokens":821,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbd916c9-65cb-4ab5-bb81-2cf8214fc421","uuid":"b4f19826-7bec-42f7-a021-fffd201b2dc5","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:01:24.881Z","request_id":"req_011CgDgyfeBrptRU77NjuW28"}
